    {
      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "मानपदवी मिथ्यैव किं खिद्यते । There are also other differences.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "Mr. Telang.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 28. चापलम्-rashness, over-haste or the folly of &c. नानारस-",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "the various sentiments which are the very essence of poetry.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "विकल्प—doubts, conflicting ideas; see also sl. 70.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 29 Cf. with this supra Mis. sl. 8. भव्यं-भवतीति; Pan. III. 4.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "68. That which becomes or exists prominently; hence excellent,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "rich. कदशन—कुत्सितमशनम् । कदशित would better keep symme-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "try with भुक्तं. वासर—वासयतीति fr. वस् cau. + अर by Un. III.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "132. सितमहत्—white and costly ( being silken ). एका भार्या–what",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "if your possessions are restricted to one wife ( and nothing else",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "i. e. if you are absolutely poor ). शतगुण &c.—गुणित multiplied;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "the whole means ‘what if you have an immense fortune.’ The",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "translation follows Ramarshi here. “On the first line Râmarshi’",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "adds आहारस्य गिलितस्यैकरूपत्वादित्यर्थः; similarly on the second",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "देहाच्छादनस्यैकरूपत्वात्, on the third भोगस्यैकरूपत्वादवसाने विरस-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "त्वाच्च, on the last देहस्य नश्वरत्वे एकत्वानेकत्वभ्रमणे को विशेषः । एतेन",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "रसस्पर्शादयः पदार्थाः सर्वेप्यनित्या इति भावः । ’—Telang.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 30. कामदुघा—‘दुहः कब्घश्च’ Pân. III. 2. 70. इति कप् ( अ )",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "प्रत्ययः घादेशश्च । fulfilling all desires. The thought has been",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "expressed more than once in this S'ataka.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 31. Cf. with this sl. 95. कन्दुक—a pillow; it properly",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "means a small round pillow for the cheek. दिक्कान्ताभिः &c.—a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "highly poetical line. भिक्षु—an ascetic, a devotee; and not neces-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "sarily a Budhistic mendicant.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 32. वक्त्रमीक्षसे-see sl. 26; Mis. 12 प्रत्याशा hopes, expecta-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "tions. Here the poet envies the happy lot of the deer. Cf. the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "idea in Vai. S'a. sl. 98. fig. अप्रस्तुतप्रशंसा.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r8",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 33. समारम्भ—attempts well-made, undertakings properly",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "commenced. Cf. Bg. IV. 19. पशु-as one not becoming wiser",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "by experience. शतधा न दीर्णम्–The many calamities with which",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "worldly life is fraught ought to rend the heart.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r9",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 34. This sl. occurs in the Mrch. मदयन्ति—i. e. by their",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
